  id: Anus
  partName: Anus
  descriptionChunks:
  - The anus is the terminal opening of the digestive tract through which fecal matter
    is expelled from the body. It is surrounded by sphincter muscles that control
    the release of waste, allowing voluntary and involuntary regulation.
  - This structure plays a critical role in maintaining digestive efficiency and
    waste elimination. Proper functioning of the anus ensures removal of indigestible
    materials, supporting overall metabolic balance and preventing accumulation of
    harmful substances within the body.
